{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Complete the week of this one.</b> It is attached — for it is punctuated with a ḥataf: the week of this one, and these are the seven days of the feast. In the Jerusalem Talmud in Mo'ed Katan. (And one cannot say an actual week, for if so it should have been punctuated with a patach under the shin; and furthermore שָׁבוּעַ is masculine, as it is written ״שִׁבְעָה שָׁבֻעֹת תִּסְפָּר לָךְ״; therefore it does not mean 'week' but 'seven' — שטיי״נא בְּלַעַז.)" "<b>and we will give her to you.</b> Plural form, like נֵרְדָה and נָבְלָה and נִשְׂרְפָה (Genesis 11) — so too this is a plural form: וְנִתֵּן." "<b>also this one.</b> Immediately after the seven days of the feast, and you shall work after her marriage."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The la'az שטיי״נא is Old French semaine (or a dialectal form), 'week'; Rashi brings it to identify the word he is rejecting as the meaning."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:09.999318834Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}